WEBVTT

00:00:01.270 --> 00:00:07.490
We've constructed a bomb with a protective 
shell hardened with mithril to critical mass.

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:12.760
With it, we can defeat the Basilisk.

00:00:40.790 --> 00:00:42.660
Mistilteinn signal lost.

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:45.460
Mistilteinn annihilated.

00:00:45.860 --> 00:00:47.970
A new exit wound has been confirmed.

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:53.110
Tear?

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:54.450
Tear!

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:57.040
Tear-san!

00:00:57.040 --> 00:00:58.050
Tear-chan!

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:31.870
It's hot.

00:01:31.870 --> 00:01:34.990
It's calling me.

00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:47.140
Tear!

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:53.970
Tear-chan.

00:01:53.970 --> 00:01:55.050
Shinomiya-sensei.

00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:56.660
To the medical office, quickly.

00:01:56.660 --> 00:01:57.440
Right.

00:02:27.820 --> 00:02:34.120
<b><i>Unlimited Fafnir</i></b>

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:46.460
<b>Red Catastrophe</b>

00:03:45.140 --> 00:03:47.750
A third eye?

00:03:47.750 --> 00:03:52.250
<i>Yes. I'll send an image, 
along with other data.</i>

00:03:57.190 --> 00:04:01.850
<i>After all the sacrifice, this is how it ends.</i>

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:05.910
No, that's not true.

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:11.230
The Basilisk must have opened its 
third eye because it was desperate.

00:04:14.190 --> 00:04:17.090
<i>That means nothing if it can't be defeated.</i>

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:21.280
<i>How is the girl with the 
color-changed Ryumon?</i>

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:23.010
She's resting.

00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:24.420
In the medical office.

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:28.070
You're not going to tell me 
to give her to NIFL, are you?

00:04:28.070 --> 00:04:29.010
Nii-san.

00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:33.740
<i>Tell her I'm sorry we couldn't live up 
to her words of encouragement.</i>

00:04:34.850 --> 00:04:36.500
Major General Dylan.

00:04:37.420 --> 00:04:39.370
<i>I wish you all luck.</i>

00:04:45.640 --> 00:04:46.940
Are you sure about this?

00:04:47.480 --> 00:04:51.310
Shouldn't we dispose of the girl 
with the color-changed Ryumon?

00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:55.860
It was us at NIFL who
captured her to begin with.

00:05:42.690 --> 00:05:44.820
According to NIFL's latest data,

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:49.360
the third eye has a firing range 
of approximately ten kilometers,

00:05:49.360 --> 00:05:50.820
twice that of normal.

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:53.170
They've determined that 
within seconds of exposure,

00:05:53.170 --> 00:05:55.810
several hundred million years are lost.

00:05:55.810 --> 00:05:57.140
Several hundred million?

00:05:57.140 --> 00:06:01.050
A normal Catastrophe takes 
2,000 years in a second.

00:06:01.050 --> 00:06:03.370
That wouldn't even leave any bones,

00:06:03.370 --> 00:06:04.890
let alone time to grow old.

00:06:04.890 --> 00:06:06.670
That's not a problem.

00:06:07.270 --> 00:06:11.440
2,000 years and several 
hundred million years

00:06:11.440 --> 00:06:13.140
are not much different to us.

00:06:13.140 --> 00:06:14.820
Exactly.

00:06:14.820 --> 00:06:16.930
It doesn't change our strategy.

00:06:17.500 --> 00:06:22.140
We'll attack its diamond scales from 
a blind spot out of its attack range,

00:06:22.140 --> 00:06:26.110
so quickly that it has no time to respond.

00:06:27.020 --> 00:06:31.510
The Basilisk is currently 150 
kilometers away from the island.

00:06:32.420 --> 00:06:38.290
We'll begin attacking it when 
it's six kilometers away.

00:06:38.290 --> 00:06:39.920
Six kilometers?

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:43.300
Won't it spot us if we don't start sooner?

00:06:43.800 --> 00:06:45.740
We'll be on the other side of the mountain,

00:06:45.740 --> 00:06:47.580
so it won't see us.

00:06:47.920 --> 00:06:51.320
And as you know, Earth is round.

00:06:51.620 --> 00:06:53.600
After a certain distance,

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:56.590
anything on the surface is 
hidden below the horizon.

00:06:56.590 --> 00:06:59.740
It becomes invisible, Iris Freyja.

00:07:00.210 --> 00:07:04.500
A person standing on the coast could 
be spotted at five kilometers, at best.

00:07:05.300 --> 00:07:09.490
Given the Basilisk's size, they would be 
visible at around ten kilometers.

00:07:09.780 --> 00:07:11.950
I thought it'd be more.

00:07:15.630 --> 00:07:18.500
We'll be using two obstacles for this operation:

00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:20.940
the volcanic island and the horizon.

00:07:21.570 --> 00:07:24.260
You guys will be on standby on 
the other side of the island.

00:07:25.890 --> 00:07:29.530
The commanding vessel will take 
Tear Lightning northward

00:07:29.530 --> 00:07:32.500
along the horizon line.

00:07:33.090 --> 00:07:37.970
And the Basilisk will react to this 
ship carrying Tear-san, of course.

00:07:37.970 --> 00:07:39.110
Yes.

00:07:39.110 --> 00:07:42.260
As soon as its attention is diverted from the island,

00:07:42.350 --> 00:07:45.790
you will all attack at once from the other side.

00:07:45.790 --> 00:07:49.050
You'll fire at it through the island.

00:07:49.980 --> 00:07:52.010
Through the island?

00:07:52.490 --> 00:07:56.680
This operation will require a 
massive amount of dark matter.

00:07:56.680 --> 00:07:59.420
Therefore, you will attack in pairs.

00:07:59.420 --> 00:08:01.780
The pairs will be as follows:

00:08:01.780 --> 00:08:04.960
Mononobe Mitsuki, Ariela Lu.

00:08:04.960 --> 00:08:05.770
Yes.

00:08:05.770 --> 00:08:08.990
I just send you my dark matter, right?

00:08:08.990 --> 00:08:09.960
Got it.

00:08:10.490 --> 00:08:13.550
Thank you, Ariela-san.

00:08:13.940 --> 00:08:16.940
Lisa Highwalker, Ren Miyazawa.

00:08:16.940 --> 00:08:17.570
Yes.

00:08:17.570 --> 00:08:18.510
Okay.

00:08:18.510 --> 00:08:21.920
But, Lisa, what about your injury?

00:08:23.800 --> 00:08:28.180
I promised Tear-san that I'd be better 
by the time we start the operation.

00:08:28.920 --> 00:08:30.580
I'm so glad, Lisa-chan.

00:08:30.580 --> 00:08:31.650
That's impressive.

00:08:32.050 --> 00:08:34.850
It doesn't make me happy 
to be complimented by you.

00:08:35.410 --> 00:08:37.930
This is a promise I made with Tear-san.

00:08:40.750 --> 00:08:41.420
Right.

00:08:42.040 --> 00:08:42.580
Next.

00:08:43.020 --> 00:08:45.650
Fyril Crest, Tachikawa Honoka.

00:08:46.690 --> 00:08:47.710
I'll do my best.

00:08:47.710 --> 00:08:48.540
Yes.

00:08:48.890 --> 00:08:51.180
You've never been in actual combat, have you?

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:53.780
Stay calm and carry out the operation.

00:08:53.990 --> 00:08:55.010
Okay.

00:08:55.490 --> 00:08:58.780
Mononobe Yuu, you'll attack 
with anti-Dragon armaments.

00:08:59.260 --> 00:09:02.890
Iris Freyja, you'll assist with dark matter.

00:09:02.890 --> 00:09:03.540
Right.

00:09:04.150 --> 00:09:07.220
I do what I did in the fight 
against the Leviathan, right?

00:09:07.220 --> 00:09:08.720
I'll do my best.

00:09:08.720 --> 00:09:09.460
Yeah.

00:09:10.020 --> 00:09:10.940
I'm counting on you.

00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:15.170
Don't let your guard down until the 
Basilisk draws its last breath.

00:09:15.170 --> 00:09:16.920
We can't discount the possibility,

00:09:16.920 --> 00:09:21.930
as NIFL did, that it has abilities 
that we don't fully understand.

00:09:22.360 --> 00:09:27.380
NIFL failed, but we have the 
incalculable power of the D.

00:09:28.020 --> 00:09:33.050
We'll end this before the Basilisk 
uses the red beam—the Catastrophe.

00:09:33.050 --> 00:09:33.920
Are we clear?

00:09:34.130 --> 00:09:35.300
Yes.

00:10:02.770 --> 00:10:04.130
Anti-gravity.

00:10:18.990 --> 00:10:20.850
<i>Leviathan's power...</i>

00:10:21.970 --> 00:10:23.860
<i>Anti-gravity.</i>

00:10:25.140 --> 00:10:29.800
You aren't the first to 
recreate a Dragon's ability.

00:10:32.320 --> 00:10:36.490
There was another who defeated a Kraken 
and gained antimatter abilities.

00:10:37.180 --> 00:10:42.370
Indeed, it was your sister, Mononobe Mitsuki.

00:10:42.370 --> 00:10:43.280
Mitsuki...

00:10:43.600 --> 00:10:48.970
So your ability to make anti-gravity particles

00:10:48.970 --> 00:10:53.260
was likely triggered by the 
battle with the Leviathan.

00:10:54.380 --> 00:10:56.670
Do you have a way to know that for sure?

00:10:56.970 --> 00:10:59.410
For sure, huh?

00:11:00.820 --> 00:11:02.140
It's an educated guess.

00:11:03.540 --> 00:11:05.140
Don't make that face.

00:11:05.700 --> 00:11:08.820
You can take comfort knowing 
it's happened before.

00:11:10.210 --> 00:11:13.740
There's no need to fear that you're different.

00:11:14.990 --> 00:11:15.810
Right.

00:11:16.560 --> 00:11:21.200
Besides, I might be able to use 
this ability to help my friends.

00:11:23.070 --> 00:11:24.920
That's the spirit.

00:11:24.920 --> 00:11:27.760
Then go work hard.

00:11:27.760 --> 00:11:28.420
Right.

00:11:30.780 --> 00:11:37.080
In fact, couldn't it be said that all 
Ds have stolen the Dragons' abilities?

00:11:38.610 --> 00:11:40.380
From the Dragons' perspective,

00:11:40.930 --> 00:11:44.860
humans are terrifying pillagers 
who've stolen their privileges

00:11:45.280 --> 00:11:47.320
one after another.

00:11:47.950 --> 00:11:49.370
Perhaps.

00:11:50.240 --> 00:11:51.600
Pillagers...

00:11:54.490 --> 00:11:55.950
No need for reservation.

00:11:55.950 --> 00:11:58.540
Take from the Basilisk, too.

00:11:58.960 --> 00:12:02.980
You aren't prey. You are predators.

00:12:04.880 --> 00:12:07.500
<i>I hope it's that easy.</i>

00:12:11.250 --> 00:12:13.660
Seigin, burst!

00:12:15.630 --> 00:12:17.580
Burst! Burst!

00:12:22.130 --> 00:12:24.440
Yay! I hit them!

00:12:24.440 --> 00:12:25.220
Iris?

00:12:26.120 --> 00:12:27.940
Mononobe... Did you see that?

00:12:29.480 --> 00:12:31.650
You hit them accurately from so far...

00:12:32.310 --> 00:12:33.490
That's impressive.

00:12:36.270 --> 00:12:39.220
I'm assisting you this time,

00:12:39.220 --> 00:12:41.820
but it might be useful in some way, right?

00:12:44.500 --> 00:12:48.620
I decided I'm going to do 
everything I can, the best I can.

00:12:52.720 --> 00:12:54.080
Remember what I told you before?

00:12:55.020 --> 00:12:58.460
That you always surpass my expectations.

00:13:00.460 --> 00:13:03.910
You mean back then?

00:13:04.530 --> 00:13:06.800
You know, when you said you wanted to...

00:13:10.630 --> 00:13:16.810
I want to know more about you someday, though.

00:13:20.290 --> 00:13:25.060
I think I want you to know me, Mononobe.

00:13:30.130 --> 00:13:31.500
I guess.

00:13:32.250 --> 00:13:34.610
Just in case worst comes to worst,

00:13:34.610 --> 00:13:35.760
can I ask you something?

00:13:35.760 --> 00:13:37.010
Ask me what?

00:13:41.330 --> 00:13:42.260
Iris,

00:13:43.100 --> 00:13:47.120
are you sure it was okay to 
thank me the way you did?

00:13:47.120 --> 00:13:47.980
Thank you?

00:13:48.340 --> 00:13:51.220
You know, when the Leviathan came.

00:13:52.130 --> 00:13:54.430
After that, on the beach...

00:13:54.770 --> 00:13:57.910
Oh... Y-Yeah.

00:13:58.720 --> 00:14:03.100
I used to kiss my family to greet them,

00:14:03.100 --> 00:14:05.860
but that was on the cheek.

00:14:07.840 --> 00:14:11.520
You're the first one I kissed on the...

00:14:12.320 --> 00:14:13.430
lips.

00:14:13.430 --> 00:14:16.540
Are you sure you wanted 
to give your first to me?

00:14:17.920 --> 00:14:19.440
With you,

00:14:20.290 --> 00:14:21.420
even my second...

00:14:21.850 --> 00:14:22.840
Iris...

00:14:29.570 --> 00:14:30.100
I—

00:14:30.980 --> 00:14:32.720
N-No!

00:14:32.720 --> 00:14:34.260
Don't say it now!

00:14:34.260 --> 00:14:37.130
Wh-What was that for?

00:14:38.150 --> 00:14:41.300
If you say something that'll make me sad,

00:14:41.300 --> 00:14:44.020
I'll get really depressed.

00:14:44.580 --> 00:14:47.580
I won't be able to do my job when I need to.

00:14:47.970 --> 00:14:49.250
No, but...

00:14:49.250 --> 00:14:52.050
Not even if it's something happy. Not now.

00:14:53.360 --> 00:14:59.580
We both have to focus, for Tear-chan's sake.

00:15:08.900 --> 00:15:11.300
All right, Iris.

00:15:33.990 --> 00:15:35.010
Tear-san.

00:15:38.710 --> 00:15:39.480
Tear.

00:15:43.590 --> 00:15:44.550
Yuu...

00:15:45.410 --> 00:15:46.570
Lisa...

00:15:46.900 --> 00:15:50.260
We won't let the Dragon have you.

00:15:52.310 --> 00:15:56.100
I know it's painful, but hang 
in there a little longer.

00:15:59.130 --> 00:16:02.710
I'm going to wait for my husband.

00:16:03.900 --> 00:16:06.330
That's a woman's fortitude.

00:16:07.190 --> 00:16:09.610
Please do that, Tear.

00:16:10.240 --> 00:16:13.020
I promise we'll defeat the Basilisk and be back.

00:16:16.690 --> 00:16:17.940
It's time.

00:16:17.940 --> 00:16:19.490
We're counting on you all.

00:16:19.860 --> 00:16:20.970
Right.

00:16:24.550 --> 00:16:25.460
Yuu.

00:16:28.040 --> 00:16:29.380
Good luck.

00:16:30.170 --> 00:16:30.870
Yeah.

00:16:40.840 --> 00:16:44.250
Basilisk at fifteen kilometers.

00:16:44.730 --> 00:16:45.940
Begin the operation!

00:17:43.400 --> 00:17:45.890
Basilisk changing course 
towards east-northeast.

00:17:45.890 --> 00:17:47.530
It's coming after us.

00:17:53.830 --> 00:17:54.600
Breunig.

00:18:10.530 --> 00:18:12.450
Come, Necronomicon.

00:18:29.500 --> 00:18:30.540
Gungnir.

00:18:47.930 --> 00:18:49.560
Let's go, Iris.

00:18:49.560 --> 00:18:50.060
Okay.

00:18:55.330 --> 00:18:58.390
Offering: Strength.

00:18:58.390 --> 00:19:00.820
Requesting: Destruction.

00:19:01.330 --> 00:19:03.480
Anti-Dragon armament, Marduke!

00:19:03.930 --> 00:19:05.960
Primary cannon, Babel!

00:19:28.240 --> 00:19:31.410
Basilisk approaching six kilometers.

00:19:35.430 --> 00:19:37.690
Ariela-san, please.

00:19:37.690 --> 00:19:39.010
Leave it to me.

00:19:48.470 --> 00:19:49.830
Please.

00:19:49.830 --> 00:19:50.650
Right!

00:20:03.880 --> 00:20:05.080
Wow...

00:20:06.820 --> 00:20:08.520
There's so much coming in.

00:20:09.640 --> 00:20:11.500
Let's pierce it.

00:20:19.530 --> 00:20:20.860
Now, Iris.

00:20:21.230 --> 00:20:21.820
Okay.

00:20:31.860 --> 00:20:34.690
Basilisk at six kilometers.

00:20:35.930 --> 00:20:37.210
Begin countdown.

00:20:37.640 --> 00:20:44.340
Nine, eight, seven, six, five...

00:20:49.160 --> 00:20:53.910
Tear-san, I'll end your suffering now.

00:21:00.130 --> 00:21:05.400
...four, three, two, one.

00:21:06.520 --> 00:21:07.210
Fire!

00:21:11.320 --> 00:21:12.200
Fire!

00:21:37.000 --> 00:21:39.250
The Basilisk is intercepting 
with its third eye!

00:21:39.470 --> 00:21:40.210
What?!

00:21:48.440 --> 00:21:49.570
What?

00:21:51.470 --> 00:21:52.090
No!

00:21:54.180 --> 00:21:55.290
It can't be!

00:23:39.810 --> 00:24:09.670
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:23:41.020 --> 00:23:45.320
I remember the day I first 
stood in front of all of you.

00:23:45.980 --> 00:23:48.090
I didn't fit in with the rest of the class.

00:23:48.090 --> 00:23:52.950
It was you, Yuu-san,
who called out gently to me.

00:23:54.460 --> 00:23:58.910
Everyone, it was only for a 
short while, but thank you.

00:23:59.950 --> 00:24:04.430
Next time on <i>Unlimited Fafnir</i>: 
"Mistilteinn Falls."

00:24:05.070 --> 00:24:09.670
Yuu-san, we'll meet again 
somewhere, won't we?

00:24:09.670 --> 00:24:24.870
<b>Illustration: Izumi Tsubasu</b>
